      "writtenOn": "2023-06-28T16:43:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is returning a copy of the vector, which was already safe (the caller could mutate it, but it was a copy so it didn\u0027t matter either way) but not very efficient.\n\nWe might have done better to return a `const std::vector\u003cSkRuntimeEffect::ChildPtr\u003e\u0026` instead. That\u0027d avoid a copy and give the caller an immutable reference to the vector. (`operator[]` on a const vector returns a const reference.)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 67,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 67,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "14e3ebd155c6569cc49dbabe777e06326b0e7731",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
